<title>NORWAY: Transocean 9-month profits rise.</title>
<headline>Transocean 9-month profits rise.</headline>
<dateline>OSLO 1996-10-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Nine months to September 30.</p>
<p>				(million of crowns unless stated)</p>
<p>Operating revenues	     2,330	vs	 2,318</p>
<p>Operating result		   184	vs	    43</p>
<p>Result before minorities/taxes 446	vs   minus  94</p>
<p>Result after tax		   433	vs   minus 105</p>
<p>NOTE - Full name of drilling and offshore services company is Transocean ASA. The company merged with U.S. group Sonat Offshore Drilling Inc. on September 4 to form Transocean Offshore Inc.</p>
<p>Transocean ASA said the nine-month result included a profit of 332 million crowns from the sale of a stake in Anchor Drilling Fluids. The operating result in the third quarter included 56 million crowns in costs related to the merger with Sonat, it said. The company said it expected day rates for most of its rigs to continue to rise.</p>
<p>--Oslo newsroom, +47 22 42 50 41</p>
</text>
